.*
.* QUIAUTL: DSPAUTL (one authorization list) and WRKAUTL (the lists),
.* laid out as the V7R1M0 captures (golden/verified/oracle71/panels).
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=AUTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=FLAGCL BASETYPE='CHAR 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=ALNAME CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ALLIB CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='QSYS'.
:VAR NAME=ALOWNER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ALPGP CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='*NONE'.
:VAR NAME=ALTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=ALUSER CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=ALAUT CLASS=AUTCL.
:VAR NAME=ALMGT CLASS=FLAGCL.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=USERS VARS='ALUSER ALAUT ALMGT'.
:LISTDEF NAME=LISTS VARS='OPT ALNAME ALTEXT'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/DSPKEYS' NAME=DSPKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display detail object authorities
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F15 ACTION='CMD DSPAUTLOBJ AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.F15=Display authorization list objects
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/WRKKEYS' NAME=WRKKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPAUTL HELP=HLPDSP KEYL=DSPKEYS TOPSEP=SPACE.Display Authorization List
:DATA DEPTH=3.
:DATACOL WIDTH=22.
:DATACOL WIDTH=41.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ALNAME' VAR=ALNAME USAGE=OUTPUT.Object
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ALLIB' VAR=ALLIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:EDATAGRP.
:DATACOL WIDTH=22.
:DATACOL WIDTH=37.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ALOWNER' VAR=ALOWNER USAGE=OUTPUT.Owner
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ALPGP' VAR=ALPGP USAGE=OUTPUT.Primary group
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=USERS SCROLL=YES.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ALUSER' VAR=ALUSER USAGE=OUTPUT.User
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ALAUT' VAR=ALAUT USAGE=OUTPUT.Object Authority
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ALMGT' VAR=ALMGT USAGE=OUTPUT.List Mgt
:ELIST.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKAUTL HELP=HLPWRK KEYL=WRKKEYS TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Authorization Lists
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=LISTS SCROLL=YES EXTACT=YES.
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?CRTAUTL AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.1=Create
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD EDTAUTL AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.2=Edit
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DLTAUTL AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPAUTL AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.5=Display
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=8 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPAUTLOBJ AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.8=Display objects in list
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=9 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPAUTLDLO AUTL(&ALNAME.)'.9=Display documents/folders in list
:LISTACT HELP='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS' OPTION=13 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGOBJD OBJ(QSYS/&ALNAME.) OBJTYPE(*AUTL)'.13=Change description
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKAUTL/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ALNAME' VAR=ALNAME USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.List
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/ALTEXT' VAR=ALTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 5, 8, 9 and 13 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPDSP.Display Authorization List - Help
:P.This display shows an authorization list: who owns it, and the
authority each user on it has to the objects it secures. An X under
List Mgt lets that user add and remove users of the list. F15 shows
the objects the list secures.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPWRK.Work with Authorization Lists - Help
:P.This display lists the authorization lists. Type an option next to
a list and press Enter: 2 edits its users, 5 shows them, 8 shows the
objects it secures, 4 deletes it. Type 1 and a name on the first line
to create a list.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F11=Display detail object authorities
:PD.Display detail object authorities.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F15=Display authorization list objects
:PD.Runs DSPAUTLOBJ AUTL(&amp.ALNAME.).
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALNAME'.Object
:P.The object shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALLIB'.Library
:P.The library shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALOWNER'.Owner
:P.The owner of the objects created.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALPGP'.Primary group
:P.The primary group shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALUSER'.User
:P.The user of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALAUT'.Object Authority
:P.The object Authority of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALMGT'.List Mgt
:P.The list Mgt of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display names only
:PD.Shows the list with the names alone, so more fit on a page.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Repeat position to.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKAUTL/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ALTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKAUTL/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it. The Create
Authorization List (CRTAUTL) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Edit
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to edit it. The Edit
Authorization List (EDTAUTL) command runs for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Authorization List (DLTAUTL) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Authorization List (DSPAUTL) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Display objects in list
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to display objects in list
it. The Display Auth List Objects (DSPAUTLOBJ) command runs for the
entry.
:PT.9=Display documents/folders in list
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to display documents/folders
in list it.
:PT.13=Change description
:PD.Type 13 next to an entry and press Enter to change description it.
The Change Object Description (CHGOBJD) command is prompted for the
entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
